The first time you do serious alchemy, you're going to
convert all your potions of speed, healing, and extra
healing into full healing.  This will typically give you
a stack of maybe thirty or so potions of full healing.
If your worst attribute (that you care about) is 13ish,
which would be typical, you can dunk five of those
potions into a gainer again and Bob is your uncle.

There are exceptions, but in most games I get
the chance to do some alchemy before mind
flayers start showing up.

> and the earlier you increase your Int the earlier
> you can reliably read spellbooks

Reading spellbooks is only really helpful if you
can get acceptable spell failure rates.  Unless
you're in a primary casting role (e.g., Wizard),
metallic armor and limited experience levels
usually prevent casting anything beyond level
three until post-castle, in my experience.  For
some roles (e.g., Barbarian) there's no point
even price-checking books up until post-castle,
because even level 1 is effectively out of reach.

But yes, it depends somewhat on role.

