I agree about fire and lightning, but wands of digging can also
be used for engraving.  The engravings aren't as permanent
as burned ones, but if I understand correctly they're as good
as the ones from an athame.  You're going to be carrying a
couple of wands of digging around anyway, because they
have several other uses, and in Gehennom you generally
have the opportunity to pick up several of them *per level*,
if you want them.

If I can cast identify, I usually pick up wands of digging until
I'm carrying an abundance of them and need to dump some
weight.  Then I identify the lot and keep the ones with the
most charges, throwing the rest in any chest (so monsters
don't keep digging annoying holes in the floor with them).
That's unless I'm a Tourist, of course.  For a Tourist, the
number of charges scarcely matters at all.


